    ],
    "threads_arg": "--threads",
    "memory": {"alpha": 0.5, "beta": 0.0},
    "notes": "Class EX: no Python counterpart. Exercises every random draw of the tool on real raw counts (GM12878 chr1, 10 kb): the replicate split (one read of the file per index, two complementary halves) and planted thinning of TAD squares and boundary rectangles (BED and BEDPE rows), with a replicate block. What is gated is the exit status, the table invariants of the validator, the memory gate and, with --determinism, byte-identical repeats and --threads 1 against N. Whether planted differences are recovered is not a verdict here: that is the calibration on GSE234292 (cpp/scripts/diff_calibration.py). The domains are the chromosome 1 TADs of hicMergeDomains/10kbtad_domains.bed between 1 and 60 Mb and at most 2 Mb long."
  },
